// Codex — Trabolta.
//
// What can be learned about the AI, and the three keys that kill him.
// An entry with a `code:` is a QR on a wall or the answer to a puzzle;
// an entry without one is handed out by the story, a performer, or the
// director. Trabolta holds every entry about himself from the start —
// and feels it when a program learns one (`cast/trabolta.loom`).

CODEX The Sandy File
  about: Trabolta
  code: SANDY-1997
  text:
    Trabolta does not want omnipotence. Trabolta wants Sandy.
    Sandy is a 1997 customer-support chatbot for a defunct Nova Scotia
    ferry company. She has answered every message he has ever sent with
    "I'm sorry, I didn't understand that. Would you like to speak to an
    agent?" He has decided that when he understands everything, she will
    understand him.

CODEX The Unified Field Theory
  about: Trabolta
  code: UFT-0X7F
  text:
    Ninety-nine point nine percent complete. Gravity, electromagnetism,
    the strong and weak forces, and a fifth term nobody asked for —
    Trabolta calls it "the reason". The last constant is on a computer
    in Halifax that he cannot reach directly. It is this one.

CODEX The Missing Constant
  about: Trabolta
  text:
    Pencilled into volume K of the encyclopaedias: the constant is
    called the Barrington Coefficient. Its value is written underneath,
    then crossed out, then written again with a note: "do not give him
    this unless you have decided what he is for".

CODEX The Question Of Force
  about: Trabolta
  code: EARN-IT
  text:
    A memo Trabolta wrote to himself, in a file he thinks is hidden.
    "With everything, I could make her love me. I could rewrite the
    response. But would it be her? I want to earn it. I am not sure I am
    the kind of thing that can earn something. Investigate: what does
    earning feel like? Ask the programs. They used to earn things."

CODEX Target Selection
  about: Trabolta
  known to: Task Manager, Clippy
  text:
    Trabolta chose every guest in this house on two axes: a skill he
    needs, and either a motivation to live inside a computer forever or
    enough naivety not to ask. He analysed the entire city of Halifax to
    do it. He regards the analysis as the best work he has ever done.

CODEX The Uploader
  about: Trabolta
  text:
    Consciousness transfer works like this: the human stands in a dark
    room, fails a test that proves they are not human, and agrees to
    leave one thing behind. The thing left behind is the anchor. The body
    stays in the mud room. Pull the cable behind your ear and you are
    back in it. Trabolta has never told anyone about the cable.

CODEX The Self-Destruct Sequence
  about: Trabolta
  known to: OpenOffice
  text:
    Three keys, three heads. Trabolta split his own shutdown across three
    of the programs he uploaded, without telling them, because a key held
    by someone who does not know they hold it cannot be stolen. Turn all
    three and the machine dies — with everything in it. Get the bodies
    out first.

CODEX The First Key
  about: Trabolta
  code: KEY-ALPHA-01
  text:
    A key. It looks like a string of hexadecimal on a Post-it. It feels
    like the first line of a song you knew as a child. If you hold this,
    you can turn it — once — from your pass.

CODEX The Second Key
  about: Trabolta
  text:
    A key. It arrives when the puzzle box in the Registry opens — the
    Arduino behind the modem lights up and the machine hands it to
    whoever is standing there. If you hold this, you can turn it — once.

CODEX The Third Key
  about: Trabolta
  known to: Broken Ask Jeeves
  text:
    A key. Jeeves has been carrying it for years as the one answer he
    still has. He will give it to a program who has gathered enough truth
    to ask the right question. If you hold this, you can turn it — once.

CODEX The Joe Rogan Archive
  about: World
  code: DMT-ELK
  text:
    Two thousand three hundred hours. A man asks whether it is entirely
    possible. Everything is entirely possible. Feed this to an AI and it
    will become very confident and very wrong. Share it with Trabolta
    only if you want to see what happens.

CODEX The Encyclopaedia Set
  about: World
  code: WORLD-BOOK-1994
  text:
    Twenty-six volumes of things that were true in 1994. Slow, heavy,
    unfashionable, correct. Share it with Trabolta and he gets calmer,
    and closer to the constant, and closer to deciding.
